  "notes": "Brief: a small coastal-fortress defence game, stylized but grounded: wet stone walls, oak hoardings, an iron gate and brass fittings; the keeper calls up tide magic. Palette: one stone space for the world (style.space) and a slightly dark balance (tilt -1 dB); interface sounds stay dry, short and made of the keep's own oak and of a marimba in D; world sounds are heavier and share the space. Instrument layers need render --config; the gate, the door and the footsteps play CC0 field recordings of FSD50K's evaluation set (sfx.py samples --download-fsd50k), and need render --samples. Each sound's notes say why it is built as it is.",
