      "notes": "An arrow striking an oak post: the wood-knock recipe adapted for the game. A higher, harder strike (the arrow's tip) and a quieter hollow body, as a solid post has little hollow behind it (at -10 dB the knock measured far peakier than the wood knocks measured during development, so the body stays at -5)."
