    {
      "id": "footsteps_stone",
      "category": "foley",
      "variants": 4,
      "trim_db": -6,
      "notes": "The keeper's shoes on the stone floors: four steps of one recording of a man walking in leather shoes across a large marble hall (FSD50K 118985, CC0; its author's note gives explicit permission to use it without attribution), one step for each variant (takes with their own offsets, from the onsets the time map shows), so no two steps in a row are the same. The hall's steady low noise (about 30 dB under the steps, 20-500 Hz) is subtracted using its quietest stretch (1.23-1.53 s), at most 15 dB, and a high-pass at 90 Hz takes the rest of the rumble; the steps chosen peak within 4.5 dB of each other. A short low thump under each adds the weight of a guard in armour. Set 6 dB under the rest of the set: a frequent sound stays understated, and as the peakiest sound here it would otherwise hold every other sound down. Needs FSD50K's evaluation set (render --samples).",
